<root BTCPP_format="4">
    <!--
        Reusable subtree: hone the sub over a labeled down-cam target using the
        WORLD-FRAME lock (LockTargetXY) instead of the incremental pixel P-hone
        (CenterCamera / HoneOverTarget). Same graceful-degrade shell as
        HoneOverTarget: if the target stays missing for miss_frames consecutive
        fresh frames or the lock exceeds the timeout, the RosTimeout/LockTargetXY
        branch fails and AlwaysSuccess lets the parent continue (dead-reckon).

        Why this exists (2026-07-26): the CenterCamera hone in HoneOverTarget
        copies the sub's CURRENT orientation into every goal, so attitude is
        unregulated; on the buoyant sub a pitch disturbance latches, tilts the
        down-cam, grows the image-x error and the relative current+step goal runs
        away -> the S2 hone diverges (ex,ey seen growing to ~0.5) and SelectTarget
        then times out. LockTargetXY commands an ABSOLUTE world point with a FIXED
        level orientation + fixed hover depth, which removes both the
        moving-setpoint windup and the pitch latch. See lock_target_xy.hpp.

        select is a PORT for the same per-target reason: the down-cam model emits
        a tiny, highly confident phantom 'table' box in a frame corner and scores
        the real table well below it, so a table caller must pass
        select="largest" to rank candidates by box area instead of confidence.
        A caller locking onto a small prop must NOT — for props the biggest box
        is not the right target. See detection_gate.hpp.

        table_z is a PORT (not hardcoded) because it is the plane the pixel ray is
        cast onto and it differs per target: the table lies ON the plane (exact),
        an object sits ABOVE it, a basket marker BELOW it. Only wired into S2
        (AcquireTable, target = table) for now, where the plane assumption is
        exactly true. gripper_x/gripper_y are sub geometry (real sub9.urdf.xacro
        mount 0.354,0), so they are constants here, mirroring how HoneOverTarget
        keeps CenterCamera's mounting map internal. Depth/level are held by the
        node (hold_z NaN = capture at start). Wrap budget is ROS time.
    -->
    <BehaviorTree ID="LockOverTarget">
        <Fallback>
            <RosTimeout msec="{timeout_msec}" ctx="{ctx}">
                <Action ID="LockTargetXY"
                        camera="{camera}"
                        label="{label}"
                        select="{select}"
                        table_z="{table_z}"
                        tol_world="{tol_world}"
                        miss_frames="{miss_frames}"
                        gripper_x="0.354"
                        gripper_y="0.0"
                        ctx="{ctx}"/>
            </RosTimeout>
            <AlwaysSuccess/>
        </Fallback>
    </BehaviorTree>
</root>
